      "side": 1,
      "message": "James: In the [console output of a failed build](https://build.aomedia.org/jenkins/job/libaom__compile/62863/arch\u003dx86_64-win64-gcc,config\u003dno-rtcd/console), the C++ compiler is identified as follows:\n\n```\n16:18:33 -- The CXX compiler identification is GNU 12.0.0\n...\n16:18:33 -- Check for working CXX compiler: /usr/bin/x86_64-w64-mingw32-g++ - skipped\n```\n\n[The changes in GCC 13](https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-13/changes.html#windows) include the following:\n\n\u003e Windows\n\u003e * The GNU threads library used by the win32 thread model has been reimplemented using direct Win32 API calls, except for the Objective-C specific subset. It requires Windows XP/Server 2003 or later. The new implementation also adds the support needed for the C++11 threads, using again direct Win32 API calls; this additional layer requires Windows Vista/Server 2008 or later. It is recommended to use a recent version of MinGW-W64 in conjunction with the win32 thread model.\n\nIs it possible to upgrade the MinGW GCC compiler to GCC 13 or later on the Jenkins machines?",
      "revId": "c6d3e8ea201aed537d8266689c52e3cc58b705e1",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
