      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Good. I suggest we apply my patch first so that we can upgrade to GoogleTest v1.17.0 and you can take your time updating the platform of our Jenkins machines.\n\u003e \n\u003e Also, I won\u0027t submit my patch to the GoogleTest upstream, especially given that the GCC team has dropped support for GCC 12. See the following note at the top of https://gcc.gnu.org/gcc-12/:\n\u003e \n\nNote https://github.com/google/oss-policies-info/blob/main/foundational-cxx-support-matrix.md still covers 7.5.0. Googletest mentions that document in their documentation: https://opensource.google/documentation/policies/cplusplus-support#c_language_standard. They do say that they want a compiler that supports C++17, so you could look at the mingw gcc-12 implementation as deficient.\n\n\u003e \u003e (This release series is no longer supported.)",
